      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.104,
            0.184,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "STATISTICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.863,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": "195"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.146,
            0.896,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": "Now n = 51. So, $\\frac{n}{2}=\\frac{51}{2}=25.5$ . This observation lies in the class 145 - 150. Then, l (the lower limit) = 145,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.249,
            0.226,
            0.895,
            0.246
          ],
          "content": "cf (the cumulative frequency of the class preceding $1 4 5 \\textrm { - } 1 5 0 )   =   1 1$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.253,
            0.771,
            0.273
          ],
          "content": "f (the frequency of the median class 145 - 150) = 18,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.278,
            0.471,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": "h (the class size) = 5."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.306,
            0.69,
            0.389
          ],
          "content": "Using the formula, Median $\\mathbf { l } = l + \\left( { \\frac { { \\displaystyle { \\frac { n } { 2 } } } - \\mathbf { c f } } { f } } \\right) \\times h .$ , we have"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.31,
            0.403,
            0.618,
            0.503
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned} & Mean  = 145 + \\left( \\frac{25.5 - 11}{18} \\right) \\times 5 \\\\&= 145 + \\frac{72.5}{18} = 149.03.5\\\\ \\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_24_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.506,
            0.546,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": "So, the median height of the girls is 149.03 cm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.531,
            0.901,
            0.57
          ],
          "content": "This means that the height of about 50% of the girls is less than this height, and 50% are taller than this height."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.574,
            0.9,
            0.614
          ],
          "content": "**Example 8 :** The median of the following data is 525. Find the values of x and y, if the total frequency is 100."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.618,
            0.775,
            0.896
          ],
          "content": "| Class intervals | Frequency |\n| --- | --- |\n| 0 - 100 | 2 |\n| 100 - 200 | 5 |\n| 200 - 300 | x |\n| 300 - 400 | 12 |\n| 400 - 500 | 17 |\n| 500 - 600 | 20 |\n| 600 - 700 | y |\n| 700 - 800 | 9 |\n| 800 - 900 | 7 |\n| 900 - 1000 | 4 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
